# Actuate the end effector.
#
# Named `Grasp` to match charter §5 and CLAUDE.md §5. It is the end-effector
# actuation skill in general, not only closing a parallel gripper: a vacuum
# end effector actuates through the same skill, which is why the goal is
# expressed as a target width and an effort rather than as a gripper command.
#
# The skill commands the gripper's ros2_control controller and nothing else
# (ADR-0022), so this action behaves identically in simulation and on hardware.
#
# WHEN THIS RESULT COMES FROM THE TWIN BOUNDARY (L5), it is an aggregate of two
# cells and not one cell's answer. `cite_twin` decides every field of it, and
# the rule is per field rather than per message:
#
#   * `result` is ranked by consequence over the sides, worst first, and every
#     side is named in `detail`.
#   * `holding` states CUSTODY and is the logical OR over the sides the goal
#     was dispatched to - somebody is holding it. A dispatched side that
#     returned no result at all counts as holding, because unknown custody has
#     to fall on the side that makes L4 escalate rather than the side that
#     makes it open a gripper (ADR-0038 decision 5, ADR-0046).
#   * `reached_width_m` and `measured_effort_n` are one side's MEASUREMENT. Two
#     grippers produce two of them and their mean is a value neither produced,
#     so L5 forwards the PLANT's whole - the side the operator is on (ADR-0044
#     clause 5) - and says so in `detail`. Where the plant returned no result,
#     none is forwarded and `detail` says that instead; the counterpart's
#     number is never reported under the plant's name.

float64 width_m                 # m, target opening between the pads
float64 max_effort_n            # N, upper bound on grip force
bool expect_object              # when true, closing to zero width is a failure:
                                # it means the gripper closed on nothing
---
ResultCode result
float64 reached_width_m         # m
float64 measured_effort_n       # N
bool holding                    # the controller stalled against something
---
float64 current_width_m         # m
float64 current_effort_n        # N
